{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-5076-r4518154","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Pico de Gallo","sourcePageId":5076,"sourceRevision":"4518154","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T16:15:32Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Pico%20de%20Gallo&oldid=4518154","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:20:18.668Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Mexican recipes","Category:Raw recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for salad","Category:Recipes for salsa","Category:Recipes using chile","Category:Recipes using cilantro","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using jalapeño chile","Category:Recipes using lime juice","Category:Recipes using tomato","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Tex-Mex recipes","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"17573bff263b4895e443a9b783220286285d700852093489f3755acc873f2212","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Mexican recipes\n| Difficulty = 1\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Sauces|Sauces]] | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Mexico|Mexican Cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Tex-Mex cuisine|Tex-Mex cuisine]]\n\n'''Pico de Gallo''' has two meanings in Mexican cuisine. The most familiar to North Americans is a fresh, tomato-based salad. It is what North Americans usually mean when talking about 'ensalada' or 'tomato ensalada'. This ensalada is never cooked.\n\nThe second meaning, more common in some regions of Mexico, is a spice mixture including salt and dried chiles, which is served over fresh fruit, often with lime juice. If one is unfamiliar with the regional origin of a recipe including pico de gallo, context may be the only way to determine which meaning is intended, though for US-Mexican dishes the uncooked salsa meaning will almost always be correct.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n*2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] fresh, seeded [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomato]]\n*½ cup chopped white or yellow [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] chopped [[Cookbook:Cilantro|cilantro]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*2 teaspoons freshly squeezed [[Cookbook:Lime|lime]] juice\n*1 teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Pepper|black pepper]]\n*1 ½ tablespoons stemmed, seeded, and [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]] [[Cookbook:Jalapeño|jalapeño]] or other [[Cookbook:Chiles|chiles]]\n*1 small clove of [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], minced\n*[[Cookbook:Hot Sauce|Hot sauce]], to taste\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n#Wash vegetables and cilantro.\n#Combine vegetables, mixing well.\n#Add salt, pepper, chiles, lime juice, and garlic.\n#Add hot sauce as desired.\n#Let stand 30 minutes to allow flavors to meld.\n\n[[Category:Mexican recipes]]\n[[Category:Tex-Mex recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for salad]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tomato]]\n[[Category:Recipes for salsa]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cilantro]]\n[[Category:Raw recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using jalapeño chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lime juice]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Pico de Gallo","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 cups chopped fresh, seeded tomato","sourceText":"2 cups chopped fresh, seeded tomato","amountText":"2 cups chopped fresh, seeded tomato","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"½ cup chopped white or yellow onion","sourceText":"½ cup chopped white or yellow onion","amountText":"½ cup chopped white or yellow onion","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 tablespoons chopped cilantro","sourceText":"2 tablespoons chopped cilantro","amountText":"2 tablespoons chopped cilantro","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"½ teaspoon salt","sourceText":"½ teaspoon salt","amountText":"½ teaspoon salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"2 teaspoons freshly squeezed lime juice","sourceText":"2 teaspoons freshly squeezed lime juice","amountText":"2 teaspoons freshly squeezed lime juice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 teaspoon ground black pepper","sourceText":"1 teaspoon ground black pepper","amountText":"1 teaspoon ground black pepper","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1 ½ tablespoons stemmed, seeded, and minced jalapeño or other chiles","sourceText":"1 ½ tablespoons stemmed, seeded, and minced jalapeño or other chiles","amountText":"1 ½ tablespoons stemmed, seeded, and minced jalapeño or other chiles","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"1 small clove of garlic, minced","sourceText":"1 small clove of garlic, minced","amountText":"1 small clove of garlic, minced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"Hot sauce, to taste","sourceText":"Hot sauce, to taste","amountText":"Hot sauce, to taste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Wash vegetables and cilantro.","sourceText":"Wash vegetables and cilantro.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Combine vegeta